  interactDistance: 5
  gazeRadius: 0.35
  displayName: 
  narration: Nikolai and I, the summer our father had us photographed in our sailor suits, as though the navy were ever going to want either of us. He's the younger one, scowling at the camera -- he hated sitting still even then. I did not know, looking at this, how little time we actually had.
